.TH CTPOOL_FUTURE_GET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ctpool_future_get \- block until the future has a result
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadpool.h>

void *ctpool_future_get(ctpool_future *f);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Blocks until the associated task has finished executing, then returns
the void* value returned by the task function. If the task was
cancelled due to ctpool_shutdown_immediate the return value is NULL
and ctpool_future_cancelled(f) will return true.

Does not free the future. The caller must call ctpool_future_free
after retrieving the result.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
f   Future handle (NULL is a no-op that returns NULL)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The void* value returned by the task function, or NULL if the future
was cancelled or f is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_submit_future (3),
.BR ctpool_future_done (3),
.BR ctpool_future_cancelled (3),
.BR ctpool_future_free (3)
